() '
(live-use.md) '
() '
(Live use) '
() '
(Status: written for Beta 1 \(Plow\).) '
() '
(The live user is cyberdeck with password cyberdeck, and that account can use sudo without) '
(a password. The installed account cannot. Project Nomad Setup does not auto-start on the) '
(live desktop. The menu entry still opens it.) '
() '
(The desktop uses Daybreak or Nightwatch from the clock. The manual icon is on the desktop.) '
(Support Cyberdeck OS is in the application menu. The Conky HUD shows CPU, battery, and) '
(network when those devices exist.) '
() '
(The live firewall drops incoming traffic and allows outgoing traffic. Chrome installs) '
(itself when the network is up. The larger Alpha 3 apps install from Install Extras or the) '
(background timer.) '
() '
(This guide is licensed under [CC BY 4.0]\(../../LICENSE-docs\).) '
() '
(updates.md) '
() '
(Updates) '
() '
(Status: written for Beta 1 \(Plow\).) '
() '
(unattended-upgrades installs Debian security and stable updates. It does not reboot the) '
(machine for you. Backports stay available for the kernel, Mesa, and most firmware.) '
(firmware-mediatek stays on Debian 13.) '
() '
(Flatpak updates run from a daily timer. Discover shows package and Flatpak updates. Apt) '
(takes a Snapper snapshot before it changes packages.) '
() '
(Google Chrome, Docker CE, Brave, Signal, VS Code, VirtualBox, and Grok Bot update from) '
(their own signed repositories after Install Extras has added those repositories.) '
() '
(This guide is licensed under [CC BY 4.0]\(../../LICENSE-docs\).) '
() '
(repair-rollback.md) '
() '
(Repair and rollback) '
() '
(Status: written for Beta 1 \(Plow\).) '
() '
(At the installed GRUB menu, the advanced or main list includes snapshot entries from) '
(grub-btrfs after apt has taken a snapshot. Booting a snapshot returns the Btrfs root to) '
(that moment. Data you stored only on /library is not inside the root snapshot.) '
ET
endstream
endobj
