() '
(If the 7.3 kernel will not boot or Wi-Fi will not associate, choose the 6.12 kernel line) '
(instead of a snapshot. That kernel stays installed next to the backports kernel.) '
() '
(This guide is licensed under [CC BY 4.0]\(../../LICENSE-docs\).) '
() '
(maintenance.md) '
() '
(Maintaining the OS and Nomad) '
() '
(Status: written for Beta 1 \(Plow\).) '
() '
(Wi-Fi) '
() '
(The image turns Wi-Fi power saving off \(wifi.powersave = 2\) and sets options mt7921e) '
(disable_aspm=1 for the MediaTek MT7922. Scans and connections use one stable MAC) '
(\(wifi.scan-rand-mac-address=no and wifi.cloned-mac-address=stable\). MediaTek firmware) '
(stays on Debian 13, not backports.) '
() '
(On a WPA2/WPA3 mixed router such as Starlink, if the link drops after it associates, edit) '
(the connection and set security to WPA2 \(wpa-psk\). Forget the network once after upgrading) '
(so the stable MAC is saved.) '
() '
(If the backports kernel still cannot join, boot the menu line that contains 6.12.) '
() '
(Clock and wallpaper) '
() '
(Daybreak \(light\) runs from 06:30 until 18:30 in the timezone the desktop is using.) '
(Nightwatch is every other time. The switch runs at login, again within 15 seconds of a) '
(clock or timezone change, and after the machine resumes. The choice is logged in) '
(~/.local/share/cyberdeck-theme.log.) '
() '
(9:00 America/Chicago is Daybreak. 21:00 America/Chicago is Nightwatch.) '
() '
(Time sync) '
() '
(systemd-timesyncd is installed and enabled. System Settings can turn NTP on. If it still) '
(says it cannot change NTP, run timedatectl set-ntp true.) '
() '
(Manual) '
() '
(The desktop icon Cyberdeck OS Manual opens the PDF in Okular. Okular is the default PDF) '
(application.) '
() '
(Snapshots) '
() '
(Snapper keeps the 4 newest numbered snapshots \(NUMBER_LIMIT=4\), which is two pre/post) '
(pairs from apt. Apt takes a snapshot before it changes packages.) '
ET
endstream
endobj
