() '
(Ollama has no apt repository. Project Nomad runs the ollama/ollama container on) '
(127.0.0.1:11434. The first-boot installer pulls llama3.2:3b. Tags containing -text- are) '
(base models and produce gibberish. Do not select them. DeepSeek R1 remains available if) '
(you pull it yourself.) '
() '
(This guide is licensed under [CC BY 4.0]\(../../LICENSE-docs\).) '
() '
(drives.md) '
() '
(Drives and Project Nomad) '
() '
(Status: written for Beta 1 \(Plow\).) '
() '
(Project Nomad Setup asks where /library lives, writes it to fstab by UUID, and orders) '
(Docker after that mount. It then starts Nomad admin on port 8080, Open WebUI on) '
(127.0.0.1:3000, Ollama on 127.0.0.1:11434, Dozzle logs on 127.0.0.1:9999, and Qdrant on) '
(127.0.0.1:6333.) '
() '
(It also starts the Supply Depot apps except Vaultwarden: Kiwix \(8090\), Kolibri, Flatnotes,) '
(CyberChef, Stirling PDF, File Browser, Calibre Web, IT Tools, Excalidraw, Homebox,) '
(Jellyfin \(8490\), LibreTranslate, Meshtastic Web \(9443\), and MeshCore Web. Their data) '
(directories are under /library/nomad/storage. Qdrant's directory is mode 777 so the) '
(container can write it.) '
() '
(The firewall allows those published LAN ports only from 192.168.0.0/16 and 10.0.0.0/8.) '
(Ollama, Open WebUI, Dozzle, and Qdrant stay on localhost.) '
() '
(The default model pull is llama3.2:3b. After Qdrant answers http://127.0.0.1:6333/healthz,) '
(upload a document in the Knowledge Base and ask the 3b model about it.) '
() '
(This guide is licensed under [CC BY 4.0]\(../../LICENSE-docs\).) '
() '
(meshtastic.md) '
() '
(Meshtastic) '
() '
(Status: written for Beta 1 \(Plow\).) '
() '
(meshtasticd is installed from the Meshtastic repository configured for Debian 13.) '
(Meshtastic Web is one of the Supply Depot containers, published on port 9443 for the local) '
(network. MeshCore Web is started on port 9444 when its image can be pulled. Vaultwarden is) '
(not installed.) '
() '
(This guide is licensed under [CC BY 4.0]\(../../LICENSE-docs\).) '
() '
(ham-tools.md) '
() '
ET
endstream
endobj
